  "description": "London Plane- Fell Undestanding this tree was in the tree preservation order where many trees where included, Order No 26/1997 /T20 Whilst the tree adds to the amenity of the area and is valuable in many ways, it has now clearly outgrown the small front garden and is impeding access to the property significantly. So much so, that the resident now has had to partially remove the boundary fence in order to access their property with childrens pushchairs and is now crossing the front garden of no10 Westbridge Road. The owner of the property propose to plant a more suitable tree that will not out grow its position so drastically. Such as Liquidambar styraciflua 'slender silhouette'",
